{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3RDooa33BV3VHJL5FtR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FTePCdi8NrofgWDwdMRdTw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"SSR tests (`npm run test:ssr`) run under Node with no DOM. Browser\ntests (`npm test`) require `npm run typecheck` to pass first. Both\nsuites must stay green. tapout serves on a fixed port (8123), so two\nbrowser runs at once fail with `EADDRINUSE`; wait for the port to free.\ntapzero's `t.throws` returns a Promise, so a sync test asserting a\nthrow should use `try`/`catch` and `t.ok`.\nsuites must stay green: `npm run gate` runs them with every other\ncheck, in cost order. Build runs before typecheck there because\n`test/types.ts` resolves `microtags` to `dist/`. Playwright is not in\nthe gate.\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"SSR tests (`npm run test:ssr`) run under Node with no DOM. Browser\ntests (`npm test`) require `npm run typecheck` to pass first. Both\nsuites must stay green: `npm run gate` runs them with every other\ncheck, in cost order. Build runs before typecheck there because\n`test/types.ts` resolves `microtags` to `dist/`. Playwright is not in\nthe gate. tapout serves on a fixed port (8123) shared with other\nworktrees, so two browser runs at once fail with `EADDRINUSE`; wait\nfor the port to free and retry rather than killing the other run.\ntapzero's `t.throws` returns a Promise, so a sync test asserting a\nthrow should use `try`/`catch` and `t.ok`.\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"morph. A tag mismatch always `console.warn`s, then looks ahead\nthrough later siblings in the range (stepping over regions) for the\nexpected tag; if none, the next item is tried against the same node. Adoption\ntests build fixtures as static HTML with `<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->` markers\nvia `innerHTML`, since browser `String(markup)` emits no markers.\nAdoption must stay passive: `_bindEl`/`_bindHost` take an `adopt`\nflag that skips static attribute values, and a bound attribute's first\nrun calls `_setAttr(..., keep)` so it writes only on a mismatch. Assert\nthis with a `MutationObserver` (`attributes`, `subtree`) attached\nbefore `mount` and read with `takeRecords()`. `npm test` serves on a\nfixed port (8123) shared with other worktrees; `EADDRINUSE` means\nanother run is active, so wait and retry.\n(`<!--[c-->` for component children) via `innerHTML`, since browser\n`String(markup)` emits no markers. Adoption alone cannot observe a\nchildren range that closes too early (the walker steps past `end`);\nre-run a region around the host so `_patch` morphs the range. `npm\ntest` serves on fixed port 8123, so parallel worktrees collide\n(EADDRINUSE): wait and retry rather than killing the other run.\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"morph. The browser parser merges adjacent text, so a raw span's\nleading text may already have been consumed by the text item before\nit: a parsed text node advances the cursor only over a text node. A\ntag mismatch always `console.warn`s, then looks ahead through later\nsiblings in the range for the expected tag, stepping over regions\n(only comments that are exactly `[` or `[c`, never stopping past\n`end`); if none, the next item is tried against the same node.\nAdoption tests build fixtures as static HTML with `<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->`\nmarkers (`<!--[c-->` for component children) via `innerHTML`, since\nbrowser `String(markup)` emits no markers. Adoption alone cannot\nobserve a children range that closes too early (the walker steps past\n`end`); re-run a region around the host so `_patch` morphs the range.\nAdoption must stay passive: `_bindEl`/`_bindHost` take an `adopt`\nflag that skips static attribute values, and a bound attribute's first\nrun calls `_setAttr(..., keep)` so it writes only on a mismatch. Assert\nthis with a `MutationObserver` (`attributes`, `subtree`) attached\nbefore `mount` and read with `takeRecords()`.\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"8123\" AGENTS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":80506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1266},"output_tokens":132,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93ae787-d8e5-4ec9-b43c-5b13cf7b4e35","uuid":"fa3b73e0-e21d-4d20-98da-60e172731adf","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:48:53.202Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3RDoWhXYKSqSCvFWwNh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FTePCdi8NrofgWDwdMRdTw":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/microtags.review-fix && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"SSR tests (`npm run test:ssr`) run under Node with no DOM. Browser\ntests (`npm test`) require `npm run typecheck` to pass first. Both\nsuites must stay green. tapout serves on a fixed port (8123), so two\nbrowser runs at once fail with `EADDRINUSE`; wait for the port to free.\ntapzero's `t.throws` returns a Promise, so a sync test asserting a\nthrow should use `try`/`catch` and `t.ok`.\nsuites must stay green: `npm run gate` runs them with every other\ncheck, in cost order. Build runs before typecheck there because\n`test/types.ts` resolves `microtags` to `dist/`. Playwright is not in\nthe gate.\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"SSR tests (`npm run test:ssr`) run under Node with no DOM. Browser\ntests (`npm test`) require `npm run typecheck` to pass first. Both\nsuites must stay green: `npm run gate` runs them with every other\ncheck, in cost order. Build runs before typecheck there because\n`test/types.ts` resolves `microtags` to `dist/`. Playwright is not in\nthe gate. tapout serves on a fixed port (8123) shared with other\nworktrees, so two browser runs at once fail with `EADDRINUSE`; 