{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3RFsy9qKLmR8VQQzv66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed all three findings and committed each one separately. The final runs all pass: `npm test` (440/440), `npm run test:ssr` (114/114), lint, and size-limit. The working tree is clean apart from the notes file.\n\n1. **Raw text after text** (`src/htm.browser.ts`). When adoption walks a `raw()` value, a text node in it now only consumes a text node from the page. If it meets an element, the browser has already merged that text into the text before it. The new test is the review's case: `<p>Price: &euro;5<button>…`. It failed first with 1 warning and 0 clicks, and now passes with no warnings and the click bound.\n2. **Lookahead leaving its range.** The lookahead now only steps over comments that are exactly `[` or `[c`. It also stops if a jump lands on the range's `end`. The new test puts a `<!--[if IE]-->` comment inside an adopted region. Before the fix, the region bound its listener to a `<b>` after the region; now it doesn't.\n3. **AGENTS.md.** I merged the two \"suites must stay green\" fragments into one paragraph and folded the dangling `<!--[c-->` text into the adoption paragraph. The port-8123 note now appears once instead of three times. I also added the gotchas from fixes 1 and 2 to that paragraph. This one is docs only, so it has no test.\n\n**Size budget raised:** fix 2 pushed the browser templater to 5306 B, just over its 5.3 kB limit. Following the spec's rule (measured size rounded up to the next 0.05 kB), I raised the limit to 5.35 kB and recorded it in `.size-limit.js` and in a new dated note in ADR-007. I tried a shared helper for the marker check to stay under the old limit, but it came out bigger.\n\n**Untested guard:** I couldn't build a test for the \"stop at `end`\" check. An unbalanced `[` inside a range also breaks the outer region's own marker lookup, so adoption gives up with \"missing region markers\" before the lookahead runs. That check is defensive, and the `[if IE]` test covers the case the review reported. This is written up in `.nightralph/notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":84654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":302},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93ae787-d8e5-4ec9-b43c-5b13cf7b4e35","uuid":"251cd3c6-450f-44c0-b9ea-c543d91e894e","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:49:17.259Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3RFsenkDn4T6iZmtEBW"}
